{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrzxrKsZwtfkxnuhFaT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `name_key` and `email_key` in `contacts/dedupe.py`. Both tests pass, the existing one and a new one I added.\n\nThere were three root causes, all in `name_key`:\n1. **Hard-coded accent list.** It only covered a handful of characters, so `ú`, `í` and every other accent were missed. In the existing test, \"Núñez\" and \"Nunez\" didn't match because `ú` wasn't in the list. It now decomposes the name (NFKD) and drops combining marks, so any accent is handled.\n2. **No Unicode normalization.** Mac text is typically decomposed (`e` plus a combining accent) and Windows text is precomposed (`é`). These never matched. NFKD normalization makes both forms identical.\n3. **`lower()` instead of `casefold()`.** `lower()` leaves \"ß\" alone, so \"Strauß\" never matched \"Strauss\". `casefold()` turns \"ß\" into \"ss\".\n\nWhitespace is now collapsed after normalization, so non-breaking spaces also match. In `email_key` I added NFKC normalization and swapped `lower()` for `casefold()`. This wasn't one of the reported causes, but it keeps email matching consistent with names.\n\nThe first-seen record still survives. The new test, `test_nfd_and_eszett_merge`, covers decomposed accents, \"ß\" vs \"ss\", a non-breaking space, and email case. I added it to `tests/test_dedupe.py` and left the existing reproduction unchanged.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14226,"cache_read_input_tokens":34982,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14226},"output_tokens":507,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa29c0fa-4f02-4b4e-a854-9a3